      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-08-11</title>\n    <style>\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            color: #000000;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n            font-size: 13px;\n        }\n\n        a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .container {\n            max-width: 1400px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 0 10px;\n        }\n\n        /* Header Styles */\n        header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 8px 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        .header-content {\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .logo {\n            font-weight: bold;\n            font-size: 16px;\n            color: #ffffff;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .date-display {\n            color: #ffffff;\n            font-size: 12px;\n        }\n\n        .nav-bar {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 5px 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        .nav-bar a {\n            color: #ffffff;\n            margin-right: 15px;\n            font-size: 12px;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .nav-bar a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Main Layout */\n        .main-content {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 15px;\n            padding: 15px 10px;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 1200px) {\n            .main-content {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n            }\n\n            .technical-insights {\n                grid-column: 1 / -1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            .main-content {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n\n            .technical-insights {\n                grid-column: 1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Section Styles */\n        .section {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n            padding: 12px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n\n        .section-header {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 12px;\n            padding-bottom: 8px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #ff6600;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .item {\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 12px;\n            border-bottom: 1px dotted #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        .item:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n            border-bottom: none;\n        }\n\n        /* Product/Update Item Styles */\n        .item-header {\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: flex-start;\n            margin-bottom: 6px;\n        }\n\n        .upvote {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 12px;\n            margin-right: 8px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            flex-shrink: 0;\n        }\n\n        .item-title {\n            flex-grow: 1;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        .item-url {\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-left: 5px;\n            word-break: break-all;\n        }\n\n        .item-description {\n            margin: 6px 0 8px 20px;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta {\n            margin-left: 20px;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .tag {\n            display: inline-block;\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            color: #ffffff;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            margin-right: 5px;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .source {\n            color: #828282;\n            margin-right: 8px;\n        }\n\n        /* Community Feedback Styles */\n        .feedback {\n            margin: 8px 0 8px 20px;\n            padding: 8px;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-quote {\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-source {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 10px;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-positive {\n            border-left-color: #00cc00;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-negative {\n            border-left-color: #cc0000;\n        }\n\n        .feedback-neutral {\n            border-left-color: #ff6600;\n        }\n\n        /* Footer Styles */\n        footer {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            border-top: none;\n            padding: 15px 10px;\n            margin-top: 20px;\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #000000;\n            margin: 0 10px;\n        }\n\n        .footer-list {\n            margin: 10px 0;\n        }\n\n        /* Print Styles */\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            .section {\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            a {\n                color: #000000;\n                text-decoration: underline;\n            }\n\n            .nav-bar {\n                display: none;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Responsive Enhancements */\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            .header-content {\n                flex-direction: column;\n                align-items: flex-start;\n            }\n\n            .date-display {\n                margin-top: 5px;\n            }\n\n            .item-header {\n                flex-direction: column;\n            }\n\n            .item-url {\n                margin-left: 0;\n                margin-top: 3px;\n            }\n\n            .item-description,\n            .item-meta,\n            .feedback {\n                margin-left: 0;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"header-content\">\n            <a href=\"#\" class=\"logo\">AgentDaily</a>\n            <div class=\"date-display\">August 11, 2026</div>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-bar\">\n        <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n        <a href=\"#updates\">Updates</a>\n        <a href=\"#insights\">Insights</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n        <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n    </div>\n\n    <main class=\"container\">\n        <div class=\"main-content\">\n            <!-- New Products Section (40%) -->\n            <section class=\"new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n                <div class=\"section\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">New Products</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://research.meta.ai/blog/introducing-muse-code-and-muse-spark-1-2\" target=\"_blank\">Meta Muse Code</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-url\">research.meta.ai</div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Meta's terminal-based AI coding agent released in beta, powered by Muse Spark 1.2 model. Handles complex software engineering tasks across large repositories including planning changes, writing code, and validating results.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Meta AI Research</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-05</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://www.group.sinch.com/media/press-releases-and-news/2026/sinch-launches-agent-tools-for-developers-and-ai-coding-assistants/\" target=\"_blank\">Sinch Agent Tools</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-url\">group.sinch.com</div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            A suite of developer integrations for building with Sinch's communication platform directly within IDEs and AI coding tools. Includes IDE extensions for VS Code and JetBrains, simulator mode for testing without account setup, and MCP server compatible with Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and ChatGPT Desktop.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Sinch Press Release</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"updates\">\n                <div class=\"section\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\">Devin: Queueing Support for Automations</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Devin introduced queueing support for automations, AI-generated review comments, and many smaller fixes and improvements.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-07</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-neutral\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"improvements in reliability and consistency, though noting Devin AI can sometimes get stuck in loops or make incorrect assumptions\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Gartner Peer Insights</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-07-github-copilot-weekly-releases-august-3/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Weekly Releases</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            GitHub Copilot released weekly updates including improvements for CLI resume and organization, VS Code review capabilities, side chats, shared sessions, and worktree workflows.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-07</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Google Workspace Plugins</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Cursor can now read, write, and act across Google Workspace with new plugins for enhanced connectivity.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-03</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://releasebot.io/updates/anthropic/claude\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code: Self-Hosted Environments Public Beta</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude Code added public beta self-hosted environments, allowing teams to run sessions on their own infrastructure with internal network access.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-positive\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"I've been using Claude to work on a medium-sized (100+kLoc) codebase, and it's a great productivity multiplier.\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Hacker News</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-neutral\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Claude Code sessions were starting at ~35K tokens\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Reddit</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://blog.mean.ceo/claude-code-news-august-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code: 8 New Features Released</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Claude Code released 8 new features including deeper agent integration and new safe mode.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">feature</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/codex-vs-claude-code-2026\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI: GPT-5.5 Default Model</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Codex CLI updated to use GPT-5.5 as the default model and began integrating GPT-5.6 Sol Ultra. Current version v0.144.0.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">release</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI: Final Preview Update Before Shutdown</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Gemini CLI shipped a preview update with core reliability fixes, security improvements, enhanced context handling. The tool was officially shut down on June 18, 2026, replaced by Antigravity CLI.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">bugfix</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-08-01</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-31-upcoming-august-2026-model-deprecations-in-github-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Upcoming Model Deprecations</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            GitHub announced that several Copilot models will be deprecated starting September 1, 2026, affecting Copilot Chat, inline edits, Ask mode, and Agent modes.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">announcement</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2026-07-31</span>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"End of an Era... Copilot is DEAD\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Reddit</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Users are complaining about significant price increases (Opus model reportedly ~2x the price)\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Reddit</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-neutral\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Discussions about switching to cheaper models for lower-level tasks\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Hacker News</div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"feedback feedback-negative\">\n                            <div class=\"feedback-quote\">\"Users noting that new Opus 4.7 model has 7.5x requests in Pro+ but costs 4x more\"</div>\n                            <div class=\"feedback-source\">— Hacker News</div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"insights\">\n                <div class=\"section\">\n                    <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Docker and Sandboxing AI Agents</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Discussion about securing AI agents through containerization and sandboxing techniques, addressing security concerns in agentic AI development.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Software Engineering Daily</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2025-08-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/\" target=\"_blank\">AI-Powered Threats to the Software Supply Chain</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Discussion about security risks and AI-related vulnerabilities in software supply chains, examining how AI can both threaten and protect software infrastructure.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Software Engineering Daily</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2025-08-04</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://blog.google/technology/ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Announces Jules AI Coding Agent</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Google announced their asynchronous coding agent called Jules, made available to everyone through both free and paid plans.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Google</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2025-08-05</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Terminal as an Agentic Interface</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Discussion with Zach and Gregor Vand about Warp's evolution and why terminals may be better suited than IDEs for agentic AI development.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">technical</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Software Engineering Daily</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2025-08-06</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n\n                    <div class=\"item\">\n                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n                            <span class=\"upvote\">▲</span>\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://medium.com/@gauritr01/part-1-react-ai-agents-a-guide-to-smarter-ai-through-reasoning-and-action-d5841db39530\" target=\"_blank\">ReACT AI Agents: A Guide to Smarter AI</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n                            Explains the ReAct (Reasoning and Acting) framework for building smarter AI agents that combine chain-of-thought reasoning with tool execution.\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                            <span class=\"tag\">tutorial</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">Gauri Trivedi</span>\n                            <span class=\"source\">2025-08-08</span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"footer-list\">\n            <a href=\"#\">Guidelines</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">FAQ</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">API</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Legal</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Search</a>\n        </div>\n        <div>\n            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Beta</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Submission</a>\n        </div>\n        <p style=\"margin-top: 15px; color: #828282;\">\n            Compiled: August 11, 2026 | Sources: Meta AI, Sinch, Devin, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Google\n        </p>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "numLines": 640,
      "startLine": 1,
      "totalLines": 640
    }
  }
